Changes in v6.3.0:
- Necronomicurse can no longer be traded
- A message is now printed in chat whenever a player joins or leaves
- Fixed an issue where players with spaces would have their usernames displayed incorrectly in death messages
- Fixed an issue where sudo and pull commands were not working on players with spaces in their name

Changes in v6.2.2:
- Fixed an issue where getting hit would freeze the character animation for other players
- Fixed an issue where pressing the map clear button crashed the game
- Fixed a general issue regarding reconnecting in large lobbies causing a crash
- Dev:
    - PlayerAnimationChanged request has been renamed to PlayerAnimationSet
    - Added a PlayerAnimationAdded request

Changes in v6.2.1:
- Fixed an issue where certain modded characters could crash

Changes in v6.2.0:
- Player state changes will now synchronize between clients
- Improved monster intent sync
- Fixed an issue where every second player in a room would not have it's stances/visuals updated or its name/hitbox rendered
- Fixed an issue where modlist match was not working correctly with large modlists
- Fixed an issue where player usernames with spaces were not correctly showing in chat
- Fixed an issue where sending a word that contained only of "#" in chat would crash the game for other players
- Fixed an issue where The Sea of Ghosts achievement was not being counted correctly when playing solo
- Fixed an issue where the map clear button was a bit overzealous, and instead of clearing the room mark on the map, it cleared the entire room cache
    - This should fix various issues like rooms resetting on player enter or rooms not being cleared for new players that joined the run
- Mod Compatibility:
    - Skul Hero Slayer:
        - Added compatibility for the mod, including animations, skins, character icon, and nameplate
    - Downfall
        - Completely reworked custom patches for The Gremlins, fixing existing bugs and crashes and improving stability greatly
- Dev:
    - LoadSkinOnPlayer of PlayerSkin now has a base method that loads the atlas, json, and corpse resources
    - LoadSkinOnPlayer of PlayerSkin now returns bool for method success instead of void
    - Removed LoadSkinOnPlayer method overrides from AtlasSkin and SpriterSkin
    - Added extra logging to the End of Turn messages
    - Removed some dev files from the mod, slightly reducing file size
    - Added 2 new commands:
        - pull [player]
            - Pulls the player with the given player name to your current location
        - turnTimerFreezeToggle
            - Freezes/Unfreezes the turn timer for you
    - Downfall:
        - Removed DefaultPlasma method from HexaghostSkin, default plasma is now always loaded if no plasma textures were found
        - GremlinsAtlasSkin class has been renamed to GremlinsSkin

Changes in v6.1.1:
- Mod Compatibility:
    - Marisa Continued:
        - Fixed an issue where the character would crash in multiplayer

Changes in v6.1.0:
- Skins:
    - Added a new skin:
        - Reaper Ironclad
            - You can unlock this skin by participating in August, September, or October 2023 raid
- Improved stability when connecting to lobbies with large amounts of people
- Slightly improved general game stability and speed
- Updated the display name of some skins to be more valid
- Fixed an issue where switching a character in the lobby screen would not launch you with the shown skin if the skin was saved as default preference
- Fixed an issue where having a currently unloaded modded character as default would not load the starting skin for ironclad correctly
- Mod Compatibility:
    - Downfall:
        - Added custom patches for the Collector
            - Patches include the character icon, both energy orbs, and skins
        - Fixed an issue where certain Hexaghost skins would render the previous skin's plasma when they should not
    - Marisa Continued:
        - Updated to the latest version of Marisa Continued to fix crashes
- Dev:
    - ChangedMapMouseCoords request has been renamed to ChangedPlayerMapMouseCoords
    - PlayerChangedHealthStatus request has been renamed to PlayerHealthStatusChanged
    - Downfall:
        - Added NoPlasma and DefaultPlasma methods to HexaghostSkin to allow for better control of Hexaghost skins

Changes in v6.0.4:
- Fixed an issue where connecting to a lobby with a character with no skins would sometimes result in a crash

Changes in v6.0.3:
- Disabled the Crown cursor until the Achievement to unlock it is complete
- Dev:
    - Removed the OnThisTrade callback from the CustomMultiplayerRelic
    - Added methods sendNetworkMessage and sendNetworkMessageToPlayer to CustomMultiplayerPower and CustomMultiplayerRelic
        - Functionally, they are the same as P2PManager.SendData, just easier access

Changes in v6.0.2:
- Fixed an issue where the booster pack version v0.0.5 would not work with this version
- Fixed an issue where the game would crash on the cursor overview screen if you didn't have a saved default colour

Changes in v6.0.1:
- Fixed an issue where the Character customization screen would crash

Changes in v6.0.0:
- Picking up a key will now remove the possibility for others to pick up the same key again
    - Picking up the ruby key will remove the Recall option from other allies at a campfire immediately
    - Picking up the emerald/sapphire key will remove the key as the reward from all other ally screens
- Player killing a player will now print a message in chat:
    - A player killing you will say "{Player} killed you"
    - You killing a player will say "You killed {Player}"
    - A player killing a player will say "{Player} killed {Player}"
- Added a new game setting:
    - Turn Time Limit:
        - Specifies the amount of time a player has to take their turn
            - Minimum value is DISABLED and maximum is 300 seconds
            - Default value for RECOMMENDED is DISABLED and for HELL mode is 30 seconds
- Added a new customizable type:
    - Player Cursors:
        - You can now customize how your cursor looks for you and your allies
        - The selected cursor is applied game-wide, not just in multiplayer menus
        - Cursor Types:
            - base - FREE, default design
            - shiny - FREE
            - Silent's Dagger - PATREON
            - crown - ACHIEVEMENT
- The customization screen has been reworked into multiple screens:
    - Player customization screen
        - You can now see all skins and set your default skins for each character separately
    - Nameplate customization screen
        - Allows the preview of both Alive and Dead designs
    - UI customization screen
    - Mouse customization screen
        - Allows the preview of both own and ally designs
    - This update will clear the saved preset for the favourite skin/character/colour/nameplate/ui
- From this version on, you will no longer be able to connect to multiplayer if your Together in Spire version is out of date
    - Previously, you'd be able to proceed with a warning
- Misc:
    - Slightly changed the text design of the Trade shop button
- Fixed an issue where the game would disconnect without retrying to refetch room data on timeout
- Fixed an issue where disconnecting from a lobby and starting a new lobby would play the leaving animation from old players in the previous lobby
- Fixed an issue where players with a space in their username would not have their username coloured correctly in chat
- Fixed an issue where trying to connect with a older game version to a lobby would fail through Port Forwarding
- Dev:
    - Added a general 'OnReceivedNetworkPacket' callback to the appropriate locations
        - This callback is meant to provide an alternative to patching into the P2PMessageAnalyzer as a cleaner solution
    - Added a 'OnPlayerKilledPlayer' callback
    - Added a new "OpenScreen" command to debug screens
    - Removed the TextButton element, correct usage is now a Clickable element with a BoxedLabel
    - PlayerPresetSave and UIPresetSave are now singleton classes

