Changes in v5.2.4:
- Multiplayer save files now store extra data for consistency, but will be saved asynchronously
    - In total, players should notice less to no stutter on game save
- Reworked how cleared rooms are tracked
    - This should have no effect on regular gameplay where all players go together, but aims more to improve the experience of people who join after a few rooms have been cleared already
- Fixed an issue where killing the first phase of the Awakened One with poison would softlock the game
- Fixed an issue where toggling The Guardian with poison would lead to an incorrect next turn intent

Changes in v5.2.3:
- Added a queue system to Steam Networking
    - The new system should prevent packet loss when dealing with huge amounts of data
    - The new system could be quite buggy so more fixes might come out in the future if needed
- Changed the duration of ally chat bubbles from 2.5s to 4s
- Fixed an issue where monster HP values would desync massively in certain scenarios
- Fixed an issue where a revived player would not get removed from the ressurect screen list until refreshed
- Fixed an issue where connecting at the same time Draw power was applied would crash the game

Changes in v5.2.2:
- Fixed an issue where exiting the lobby would cause a crash
- Fixed an issue where clicking on a player box would cause a crash

Changes in v5.2.1:
- Having more than 11 players in a lobby will now display the total count BELOW the list of players instead of replacing it
    - Added arrows below the player count in the lobby when there's more than 11 players to be able to see all players
    - Fixed an issue where the 5th player connecting would show as duplicate in the lobby screen
- Reworked the player select screens (trading and resurrecting)
    - The super small mode has been replaced with the medium size for player counts above 11
    - Added arrows to the screen to scroll through the player list
    - Added a player name filter to more easily find players
- Player nameboxes in rooms will now have arrows to scroll for player counts above 11
- Dev:
    - Added 2 new commands:
        - Add Player command
            - Adds a dummy player with random character, name, gold, and energy to the game
            - Useful for debugging player UI/player logic
        - Verify Client Mods command
            - Checks your current mods and matches them against the online list of allowed client mods

Changes in v5.2.0:
- Completely reworked enemy intent sync with the goal of making it desync less often
    - This change is very technical and includes some back-end changes but ideally it should significantly reduce the amount of intent-related issues
- Timing out on room data will now retry the request instead of generating a room, and failing a second timeout will disconnect you
    - This should prevent the issue where rooms would refresh on ocassion with a large amount of players playing
- Fixed an issue where turn counts were not syncing for players who joined the room after the room was loaded
- Fixed issues where damaging monsters at certain times would not sync the data, leading to a temporary desync in hp values
- Fixed an issue where The Guardian going into defensive mode due to debuffs (example - Poison) would not sync
- Fixed an issue where the game would crash when marking yourself with the chat marker in the lobby

Changes in v5.1.3:
- You can now earn achievements in CUSTOM mode as long as Allow Cheats option is turned off
- Fixed an issue where targeting allies with upgraded defends was not working since v5
- Fixed an issue where the game would crash if the random character option selected a modded character without custom patches
- Fixed an issue where a single-player game would crash on Gremlin Horn trigger
- Fixed an issue where a single-player game would crash if you attempted to draw on the map
- Fixed an issue where the game would crash on steam deck when opening the map

Changes in v5.1.2:
- Implemented missing changes for the Raid Event

Changes in v5.1.1:
- Added a new Watcher skin:
    - Poolside
- Removed the option to teleport to other players when dead
    - While not buggy, this option proved to be pointles and confusing when paired with the new functionality of seeing ALLY items
- Fixed an issue where toggleable items were not working correctly
- Fixed an issue where Room nodes were not offset on X axis
- Fixed an issue where Retain cards would stack in the "hand pile" ally screen instead of being removed properly
- Fixed some issues where certain enemy attacks could get skipped/duplicated
- Dev:
    - Reworked the skin resource loading system to be more flexible and easier to expand on

Changes in v5.1.0:
- Players:
    - You can now right click on players to view their current and max hp, gold, card piles, relics, blights, and potions
- Map:
    - You can now see other player cursors when they are at the map screen
- Multiplayer Lobby:
    - Added a random option at the end of the character select
        - It will assign you a random character with a random owned skin upon embarking
- Skins:
    - Added a new Watcher Skin:
        - Poolside
            - You can unlock this skin by participating in the May, June, or July raids
- Misc:
    - Choke applied on players will now trigger whenever allies play cards
    - Changed the design of the drawing dot to be a bit sharper
    - When an ally plays a card through you your turn will now un-end
    - When your turn is forcefully ended through a card/monster, you can no longer un-end it
- Together in Spire Achievements will now be unlockable regardless of what client/content mods you have active
- Improved player targeting to fail way less often
- Improved syncing of Monster Intents - aiming to eliminate discrepancies on end of turn intent changes with some monsters
- You can now target allies with potions that have a targeter
- Fixed an issue where the Chibi Watcher skin would not apply on the own player model
- Fixed issues where game ui would be clickable under custom screens
- Fixed an issue where the mod would not launch in certain Windows language presets
- Fixed an issue where the game could crash when new players joined mid-game
- Fixed an issue where the game would crash when a Watcher player died for all players except the player who died
- Fixed an issue where the game would crash if you opened the map after reconnecting before all the other players reconnected
- Fixed an issue where the Awakened One's Powers would get removed only for the player that lands the deadly blow
- Dev:
    - Player Blights will now be synced
    - Added a WatcherSpriterSkin to do easier Spriter Skins for the watcher
    - Added callback methods for when a blight is obtained

Changes in v5.0.1:
- Fixed an issue where the game could crash when selecting the "Modlist Match" filter on the Steam Lobby List
- Fixed an issue where the first player to mark a room would have their color persist permanently even when unmarked
- Mod Compatibility:
    - Fixed an issue where none of the compatible character mods were launchable since v5

Changes in v5.0.0:
- Map:
    - Reworked the Map Mark system
    - Changed the icon for Marked Rooms
    - Holding right click will now draw on the map and also mark any rooms you hover over
    - Added a clear button that clears any marks you made
    - Map Nodes will now have their offsets synced between players
- Chat:
    - Added Chat to the game
    - You can open the chat by pressing TAB
    - It supports following effects:
        - #y, #g, #r, #b, #p - for yellow, green, red, blue, and purple word colors
        - #RRGGBB - for custom colours
        - @word@ - for shaky word effect
        - ~word~ - for wavy word effect
- QOL:
    - All RECOMMENDED reward character nameplates have been given an extra overlay on top to increase text visibility
    - The Watcher's Eye will now render in the correct position on all skins
    - The Watcher's Eye will now have unique textures for the following skins:
        - CORRUPTED
        - STREAMER
        - ROMAN
        - GHOST
        - HEARTSLAYER
    - Gremlin Horn will now un-end your turn on trigger
- Improved monster state sync
- Trade option will no longer say "Not connected to multiplayer" in certain scenarios
- Fixed an issue where the game could crash on modded when obtaining certain relics
- Fixed an issue where losing block due to teammate actions could reduce your block into negatives
- Fixed an issue where having starting relics in CUSTOM would crash your game
- Mod Compatibility:
    - All currently officially supported modded characters will now be able to use their upgraded defends to block for their allies
- Dev:
    - The list of client mods will now be grabbed from an online url at game start instead of being coded into the mod
    - Added a new CustomMultiplayerPower class with respective identical multiplayer methods found in CustomMultiplayerRelic
    - onClick method in Clickable has been renamed to onLeftClick
    - Added a onRightClick method to Clickable
    - Added a Special Action method to CharacterEntity and P2PPlayer as well as a onFFSpecialAction methods to respective classes for modded scenarios
    - Renamed all respective onAllyUsedCard methods to onAllyPlayedCard for better clarity
    - Added new callback methods
        - onTradeModifyReceivingCards
        - onTradeModifyReceivingRelics
        - onTradeModifyReceivingPotions
        - onTradeModifyReceivingGold

Changes in v4.2.0:
- Fixed an issue where enemies would not scale their damage past the first move with damage settings
- Mod Compatibility:
    - The Abyssal
        - The Abyssal has been added to the list of officially supported mods
        - Added a new REDBEARD skin for the character, as well as the Ghost, Streamer, and Heartslayer skins
